This product includes API schema definitions derived from third parties:

- The OpenAPI schemas for the OpenAI Responses and Chat Completions APIs, under
  schema/responses/ and schema/chat-completions/ (and the Zod validators
  generated from them under src/generated/), are derived from the Open Responses
  project (https://github.com/openresponses/openresponses), licensed under the
  Apache License 2.0. Those in turn model the official OpenAI OpenAPI
  specification (https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi).

- The Anthropic Messages OpenAPI schema, under schema/anthropic-messages/, is a
  hand-authored wire-shape contract based on Anthropic's public API
  documentation (https://docs.anthropic.com/en/api/messages).

The reasoning eval questions under src/reasoning/cases.ts are fixed subsets of
third-party datasets, ported from ds4-eval:

- GPQA Diamond (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Wanfq/gpqa), CC BY 4.0.
- SuperGPQA (https://huggingface.co/datasets/m-a-p/SuperGPQA), ODC-BY; mostly
  original data plus a limited amount of transformed third-party data.
- AIME 2025 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/test-time-compute/aime_2025), MIT.
- COMPSEC: reduced single-function vulnerability localization questions derived
  from public CVE writeups.

The hard suite under src/reasoning/hard-cases.ts (--eval-suite hard) likewise:

- MMLU-Pro (https://github.com/TIGER-AI-Lab/MMLU-Pro), Apache-2.0.
- OlympiadBench (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Hothan/OlympiadBench),
  Apache-2.0; English text-only rows, only the published final answers embedded.
- LiveBench reasoning (https://huggingface.co/datasets/livebench/reasoning),
  Apache-2.0; the benchmark's own output wrapper is replaced by this eval's
  answer-line instruction.
- NIST Juliet 1.3 (https://samate.nist.gov/SARD/test-suites/112), CC0-1.0;
  the cases are short locally written reductions of Juliet weakness patterns,
  not copies of Juliet test cases.

All other source code — the probe, scoring, conformance tests, capability evals,
benchmark, and CLI — is original to llmprobe.
